      "writtenOn": "2026-08-12T07:02:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "${session_num} is only set inside the FOR ${session_num} IN RANGE 2 6 loop body. If Verify KVM Is Connected And Elements Are Visible (the first assertion, before the loop) fails, the FOR loop never executes, and ${session_num} is never defined. The teardown then calls Close Sessions ${session_num} with an undefined variable, which raises a second error and masks the original failure.\n\nFix:\n```\nVerify KVM Multiple Sessions\n    [Tags]  Verify_KVM_Multiple_Sessions\n    [Teardown]  Close Sessions  5\n```\n\nOr use a constant that matches the IN RANGE 2 6 upper bound:\n```\n    [Teardown]  Close Sessions  ${5}\n```\n\nAlternatively, initialise the variable before the loop:\n```\n    VAR  ${session_num}  1\n    FOR  ${session_num}  IN RANGE  2  6\n        ...\n    END\n    [Teardown]  Close Sessions  ${session_num}\n```",
      "revId": "185863ddb4a3a5d820b25d15deb31d36c34ae116",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
